## What is AJAX?

**AJAX (Asynchronous JavaScript and XML)** is a web development technique used to **exchange data with a web server without reloading the entire web page**.

AJAX allows a web page to update a part of the page dynamically and asynchronously.

### How AJAX Works

```text
User Action
     ↓
JavaScript / AJAX
     ↓
Request sent to Server
     ↓
Server processes Request
     ↓
Response received
     ↓
Only required part of Web Page is updated
```

### Example

For example, when a user enters a search term on a website, suggestions can appear **without reloading the complete web page**. This can be achieved using AJAX.

## Difference between AJAX and JavaScript

| Basis                    | AJAX                                                                                                | JavaScript                                                                  |
| ------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Meaning**              | AJAX stands for Asynchronous JavaScript and XML.                                                    | JavaScript is a scripting/programming language.                             |
| **Purpose**              | Mainly used for communicating with a server asynchronously and updating web pages.                  | Used to add logic, interactivity and dynamic behaviour to web pages.        |
| **Page Reload**          | Can update data without reloading the complete page.                                                | Changes made by JavaScript do not necessarily involve server communication. |
| **Server Communication** | Commonly used to send and receive data from a server.                                               | By itself, JavaScript does not automatically communicate with a server.     |
| **Technology**           | AJAX is a technique that uses JavaScript along with web APIs such as `XMLHttpRequest` or `fetch()`. | JavaScript is the language used to write the program.                       |
| **Example**              | Loading new data from a server without refreshing the page.                                         | Changing text, colour, or displaying/hiding an HTML element.                |

### Conclusion

AJAX is **not a separate programming language**. It is a technique that uses JavaScript and web communication mechanisms to exchange data with a server **asynchronously** and update a web page without a complete reload.
