## What is CSS?

**CSS (Cascading Style Sheets)** is a style sheet language used to **define the appearance and layout of HTML web pages**.

CSS is used to control the **colour, font, size, spacing, background, borders, and layout** of HTML elements.

### Embedded Style Sheets

An **Embedded Style Sheet** is a CSS method in which CSS rules are written inside the `<style>` element within the `<head>` section of an HTML document.

It is also called **Internal CSS**.

Embedded CSS is useful when the styles are required for **a single HTML page**.

### Syntax

```html
<head>
    <style>
        selector {
            property: value;
        }
    </style>
</head>
```

### Example

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Embedded CSS Example</title>

    <style>
        h1 {
            color: blue;
            text-align: center;
        }

        p {
            color: green;
            font-size: 18px;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

    <h1>Welcome to IGNOU</h1>
    <p>This is an example of Embedded Style Sheet.</p>

</body>
</html>
```

### Explanation of Example

1. The `<style>` tag is written inside the `<head>` section.
2. The `h1` selector applies the CSS to the heading.
3. `color: blue` makes the heading blue.
4. `text-align: center` aligns the heading in the centre.
5. The `p` selector applies the CSS to the paragraph.
6. `font-size: 18px` changes the size of the paragraph text.

### Advantages of Embedded Style Sheets

* CSS and HTML are contained in the **same HTML document**.
* It is useful for styling **a single web page**.
* It is easier to manage than applying styles individually using the `style` attribute.
* It improves the readability of HTML compared with using many inline styles.

### Conclusion

CSS is used to control the presentation and layout of HTML documents. An **embedded style sheet** places CSS rules inside the `<style>` tag in the `<head>` section and is mainly suitable when styling a single HTML page.
