Explain the following WML elements : 3
(i) <optgroup>
(ii) <setvar>

## (i) `<optgroup>`

* The `<optgroup>` element is used to **group related options** inside a `<select>` element.
* It makes a long list of options easier to organize.
* It has a `title` attribute that specifies the name of the group.

**Example:**

```xml
<select name="course">
    <optgroup title="Computer Courses">
        <option value="bca">BCA</option>
        <option value="mca">MCA</option>
    </optgroup>
</select>
```

Here, BCA and MCA are grouped under **Computer Courses**.

---

## (ii) `<setvar>`

* The `<setvar>` element is used to **set or change the value of a WML variable**.
* It is commonly used inside `<go>`, `<prev>`, or `<do>` elements.
* It has two important attributes:

  * `name` – specifies the variable name.
  * `value` – specifies the value assigned to the variable.

**Example:**

```xml
<setvar name="username" value="Nidhi"/>
```

This statement sets the value of the variable `username` to **Nidhi**.

### In short:

* `<optgroup>` → **Groups related options.**
* `<setvar>` → **Sets or changes a variable's value.**
